<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<jmeterTestPlan version="1.2" properties="5.0" jmeter="5.6.3">
  <hashTree>
    <TestPlan guiclass="TestPlanGui" testclass="TestPlan" testname="23120274 - Spike - Category Management &amp; Verification" enabled="true">
      <stringProp name="TestPlan.comments">[DESIGN ONLY; NOT EXECUTED] Created2026-11-19 Asia/Saigon. Spike two native Thread Groups, no plugin.
Continuous baseline10VU ramp20s, then steady baseline60s (t20..80). Extra90VU ramp3s at t80, total100VU target at t83; hold60s to t143; burst group duration63s after80s delay. Baseline group continues while burst drains; recovery10VU lasts60s after observed engine active count returns exactly10 (not simply t143). Nominal end203s, plus observed drain/tail and setup/guarded cleanup. Baseline group intentionally has no fixed scheduler: gate ends after actual recovery60s;30s drain watchdog is a safety coordination limit, not a response-time SLA.
Native schedulers are approximate; actual100VU/60s and3s rise must be verified using timestamps, grpThreads/allThreads and phases; think1-2s before Login delays HTTP arrival even after thread starts. No claim RPS=VU. In-flight calls may cross boundaries; no new burst Create intent after cutoff; partial intents recovered outside measurement. Safety abort overrides all target phases.
Credentials env ESHOP_ADMIN_EMAIL/ESHOP_ADMIN_PASSWORD only. Same approved CSV hash, headers/endpoints/extractors/contract assertions/timer. JWT/ID thread-local; baseline workers1..10, burst11..100. Shared fragment copied once structurally, helper methods reused from unchanged Load/Stress. hw05.spike_reviewed,hw05.allow_mutation,hw05.isolated_sut defaultfalse.
Future non-GUI launcher must load -q test-plans/spike-results.properties BEFORE startup plus output paths unique toSpike; do not use Load/Stress launcher. Properties required in setup include epoch-ms start timestamps, thread counts and sample_variables=spike_phase,spike_cohort,spike_boundary_crossed. Additional phase labels:WARMUP/BASELINE/SPIKE_RAMP/SPIKE_HOLD/RECOVERY_TRANSITION/RECOVERY/RECOVERY_TAIL. Tag based on actual prev.startTime/endTime in postprocessor, not before think timer; no phase added to HTTP labels. Preserve failed samples, count HTTP/assertion errors independently of abort. Ignore internal/setup/teardown control samples.
Stress official37750HTTP,7550completeiterations,0errors,50workers,cleanupVERIFIED; peakbackendWS114.523MiB/machineCPU6.152percent,freeRAMmin2631MiB. Currenthardware17:00:59+07:i5-11400H6cores12logical,16122MiBtotal,4784MiBfree. These do not validate100VU or injector headroom. min_free_mib&gt;=2048 remains mandatory. Conditional design only; before anySpike require fresh preflight/read-only credential check, isolatedSUT, small pilot and backend+injector monitoring. No Spike request sent during this task.
Inherited Stress error policy:429/500/502/503/504 and allowlisted transport failures atLogin/View before mutation are FAILED samples, dependencies skipped, nextpacediteration allowed. Identity/role/account/auth401403/contract/baseline/manifest errors and unknownwrite are fatal safety abort. No retryCreate/Delete; durableintent beforewrite, confirmedID beforeDelete, baseline/refID exclusions, exactID+name absenceassertion; guarded independentrecovery refusesambiguity/references/unknownlatewrites. No prefix deletes/reset/restart. Mainworkflow has no extraownershipGET and requires isolation; CreateHTTP200 alone is not read-after-write proof. Forcedkill can skiptearDown.
Response Time Graph is an offline report view, disabled/not rendered in future non-GUI execution; clearfilename prevents writing into oldStressJTL. Listener saveconfig no bodies/headers/tokens. Safe responseMessage inherited from Stress. Main recovery is active10VU, not quietsleep; finalguardedcleanup outsidemeasurement uses unchanged Load recovery implementation. Runtime scheduling,100VU,timeout/forcedstop paths unverified. Review before pilot/execution.

Execution preparation: data/spike-profiles.json is shared source for launcher/helper/checker. Official profile unchanged. Explicit spike_mode=pilot validates ALL properties; pilot2-&gt;6-&gt;2VU: warmup2s,baseline8s,rise1s,peak10s,recovery10s,nominal31s plus drain/tails. Raw JTL properties loaded by launcher -q. Pilot results isolated from official.

Pilot-discovered scheduler fix: burst has a longer defensive scheduler (official95s afterdelay80; pilot43s afterdelay10); Groovy gate controls logical burststop143s/21s. This prevents JMeter stopping a thread early merely because its next think timer crosses the scheduler deadline. No new burst Create after logicalstop; existing work drains before active-baseline Recovery. Checker additionally validates steady-phase active counts.
</stringProp>
      <boolProp name="TestPlan.functional_mode">false</boolProp>
